// `Measure − Measure → Measure` (same dimension), SATURATING at zero — the §3 ② *reservation* case
// (reserve a measured demand from a budget). The dimension is preserved (a budget minus a demand is
// still a budget); only the magnitude changes. Fail-closed (§5): an over-reservation (`b ≥ a`) floors
// to a zero-magnitude budget the consumer reads as "no room", NEVER an underflowed huge `Nat` that
// would fabricate budget out of nothing. On saturation `a.count - a.count` is the `Nat` zero source
// (keeps both arms `Nat`, no literal).
fn measure_saturating_sub<Q, S>(a: Measure<Q, S, Nat>, b: Measure<Q, S, Nat>) -> Measure<Q, S, Nat> {
  Measure { count: if a.count <= b.count { a.count - a.count } else { a.count - b.count } }
